  "summary_en": "Law firm client alert summarising Saudi Arabia's new technical regulations for autonomous vehicles (SASO) and Saudi Highway Code Volume 801 (Roads Authority). It describes scope (SAE levels 4-5), economic operator obligations, safety annexes, and the TGA sandbox pilot, with entry into force in April 2026.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Regulations apply to SAE level 4 and 5 passenger and goods vehicles, local and imported.",
   "Economic operators (manufacturers, importers, distributors, authorized representatives) have role-specific compliance, conformity assessment and recall duties.",
   "Article 10 sets essential safety requirements; Annexes cover ADS testing, performance requirements and limited exceptions.",
   "SHC 801 sets infrastructure readiness and safety oversight requirements.",
   "TGA sandbox pilot preceded entry into force in April 2026; first permit issued to WeRide."
